          "requirement": "Exercise the supported pre-parse configuration of a parser with a caller-supplied 16-byte hash salt, including its use by hashing and inheritance by external-entity parsers.",
          "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput creates root and namespace parsers, then ParseOneInput calls XML_SetHashSalt with an unsigned-long SipHash result before XML_Parse. The parent subsequently creates external-entity parsers.",
          "failure_condition": "For any ordinary valid XML input, such as <a/>, the target has no call that supplies 16 entropy bytes. Its legacy setter fixes the high key half to zero. Thus no target call sequence exercises a caller-chosen full-width salt.",
          "alternative_paths": "Automatic generation, including the possible zero-legacy-salt route, chooses a library-generated value; it cannot exercise a caller-supplied 16-byte value. The target's other parser calls use the same ParseOneInput helper, and child parsers inherit the parent's configured key.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        }
      ],
      "decisions": [
